flowchart TB
  accTitle: Compositional ablation plan
  accDescr: The evaluation includes source-required ablations of state, authoritative control, and learning. Dependency experiments compare B2 with and without B4, B3 with native retrieval versus B1 and B1 plus B6, B2 recovery-trace admission policies for GraSP, and the B4 plus B6 interaction before staged full-composition testing.
  CORE[Three required ablation types]
  A[Remove new state object]
  B[Remove authority edge but keep logging]
  C[Remove learning update but keep transition]
  DEP[Dependency experiments]
  D1[B2 with and without B4]
  D2[B3: native retrieval vs B1 vs B1 plus B6]
  D3[B2 trace admission: none vs all vs verified only]
  D4[B4 with B6]
  FULL[Staged and full composition]
  CORE --> A
  CORE --> B
  CORE --> C
  A --> DEP
  B --> DEP
  C --> DEP
  DEP --> D1
  DEP --> D2
  DEP --> D3
  DEP --> D4
  D1 --> FULL
  D2 --> FULL
  D3 --> FULL
  D4 --> FULL
  classDef required fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.4px
  classDef experiment fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.2px
  classDef result fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px
  class CORE,A,B,C required
  class DEP,D1,D2,D3,D4 experiment
  class FULL result
